  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n`AtomWallet.owner()` at L271 has two branches:\n```solidity\nfunction owner() public view override returns (address) {\n    OwnableStorage storage $ = _getAtomWalletOwnerStorage();\n    return isClaimed ? $._owner : multiVault.getAtomWarden(); // ← external call to MultiVault\n}\n\n```\n\n`_validateSignature`, which is called by every `validateUserOp` execution, calls `owner()` at L309:\n\n```solidity\nbool sigFailed = recovered != owner(); // triggers the external call for unclaimed wallets\n\n```\nFor every unclaimed AtomWallet, `validateUserOp` reads storage from MultiVault via the `getAtomWarden()` external call. This violates ERC-4337 §6.2.\n\nThe ERC-4337 bundler storage access rule (enforced via debug_traceCall simulation by Pimlico, Alchemy, Infinitism, and all compliant bundlers) states:\n\n`During validateUserOp, an account may only access its own storage, or the storage of entities that are staked in the EntryPoint (paymasters, factories).`\n\n\n`MultiVault` is not staked in the EntryPoint — it is a plain protocol contract. Any compliant bundler simulating the UserOp will detect that validateUserOp SLOAD'd from MultiVault's storage slot and reject the UserOp before it reaches the chain.\n\n### Impact:\n\n- Every AtomWallet is deployed in the unclaimed state. This means the entire protocol's ERC-4337 infrastructure is non-functional by default. The `atomWarden` cannot use UserOps to interact with unclaimed wallets through bundlers. Sponsored transactions, paymasters, and any bundler-based gas abstraction are unavailable until a wallet is individually claimed — which itself requires a direct on-chain transaction, defeating the purpose of the AA design.\n\nThe violation disappears post-claim because `isClaimed = true causes owner()` to read from the wallet's own local storage slot instead.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nCache the atomWarden address in the wallet's own storage at `initialize()` time. `owner()` reads the cached local slot — no external call, no bundler violation:\n\n```diff\n+ address private _cachedAtomWarden;\n\n  function initialize(address anEntryPoint, address _multiVault, bytes32 _termId) external initializer {\n      address warden = IMultiVault(_multiVault).getAtomWarden();\n      __Ownable_init(warden);\n      __ReentrancyGuard_init();\n+     _cachedAtomWarden = warden;\n      _entryPoint = IEntryPoint(anEntryPoint);\n      multiVault = IMultiVault(_multiVault);\n      termId = _termId;\n  }\n\n  function owner() public view override returns (address) {\n      OwnableStorage storage $ = _getAtomWalletOwnerStorage();\n-     return isClaimed ? $._owner : multiVault.getAtomWarden();\n+     return isClaimed ? $._owner : _cachedAtomWarden;\n  }\n\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport {console2} from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport {PackedUserOperation} from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/PackedUserOperation.sol\";\nimport {_packValidationData} from \"@account-abstraction/core/Helpers.sol\";\nimport {TransparentUpgradeableProxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\n\nimport {AtomWallet} from \"src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol\";\nimport {BaseTest} from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\n\n\ncontract PoCAtomWalletBundlerViolation is BaseTest {\n  \n    function test_poc_bundlerStorageViolation() external {\n        // BaseTest.setUp() ends with resetPrank() leaving an active prank.\n        // Clear it so vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT) works correctly below.\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        /*──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n         * SETUP\n         *────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────*/\n        uint256 wardenKey = uint256(keccak256(\"poc-warden\"));\n        address wardenAddr = vm.addr(wardenKey);\n\n        // Make multiVault return our controlled warden (ownership setup only)\n        vm.mockCall(\n            address(protocol.multiVault),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(protocol.multiVault.getAtomWarden.selector),\n            abi.encode(wardenAddr)\n        );\n\n        // Deploy fresh AtomWallet backed by real protocol.multiVault\n        AtomWallet impl = new AtomWallet();\n        AtomWallet wallet = AtomWallet(\n            payable(address(new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(address(impl), users.admin, \"\")))\n        );\n        wallet.initialize(ENTRY_POINT, address(protocol.multiVault), bytes32(\"poc\"));\n\n        assertFalse(wallet.isClaimed(), \"PRECONDITION: wallet must start unclaimed\");\n        assertEq(wallet.owner(), wardenAddr, \"PRECONDITION: unclaimed owner() must call getAtomWarden()\");\n\n        // Build UserOp signed by the warden key\n        // Signing with the matching key guarantees ECDSA recovery returns wardenAddr,\n        // so execution always reaches `recovered != owner()` (L309) -- no early-return risk\n        bytes32 opHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"poc-hash\", address(wallet)));\n        bytes32 ethHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", opHash));\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(wardenKey, ethHash);\n        PackedUserOperation memory op = PackedUserOperation({\n            sender: address(wallet),\n            nonce: 0,\n            initCode: \"\",\n            callData: \"\",\n            accountGasLimits: bytes32((uint256(500_000) << 128) | 500_000),\n            preVerificationGas: 21_000,\n            gasFees: bytes32((uint256(1e9) << 128) | 1e9),\n            paymasterAndData: \"\",\n            signature: abi.encodePacked(r, s, v)\n        });\n\n\n\n        vm.expectCall(\n            address(protocol.multiVault),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(protocol.multiVault.getAtomWarden.selector)\n            // 2-arg form: asserts at least one call fires during validateUserOp.\n            // getAtomWarden() is actually called multiple times (owner() is invoked\n            // from several points in the call stack), which proves the violation is\n            // even more pervasive than a single read.\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 validationData = wallet.validateUserOp(op, opHash, 0);\n\n        // validationData == 0: signature VALID -- violation is on the happy path\n        assertEq(\n            validationData,\n            _packValidationData(false, 0, 0),\n            \"Sig must succeed -- proves violation occurs on a valid UserOp\"\n        );\n\n      \n        vm.startPrank(wardenAddr);\n        wallet.transferOwnership(wardenAddr);\n        wallet.acceptOwnership();\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertTrue(wallet.isClaimed(), \"POSTCONDITION: wallet must be claimed\");\n        assertEq(wallet.owner(), wardenAddr);\n\n        // Clear mocks, install tripwire -- any call to getAtomWarden() = test FAILS\n        vm.clearMockedCalls();\n        vm.mockCallRevert(\n            address(protocol.multiVault),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(protocol.multiVault.getAtomWarden.selector),\n            \"TRIPWIRE: getAtomWarden() called post-claim -- VIOLATION\"\n        );\n\n        // Rebuild signed op for Phase 2\n        bytes32 opHash2 = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"poc-hash-2\", address(wallet)));\n        bytes32 ethHash2 = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", opHash2));\n        (v, r, s) = vm.sign(wardenKey, ethHash2);\n        op.nonce = 1;\n        op.signature = abi.encodePacked(r, s, v);\n\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 validationData2 = wallet.validateUserOp(op, opHash2, 0);\n\n        assertEq(\n            validationData2,\n            _packValidationData(false, 0, 0),\n            \"Post-claim sig must validate without touching multiVault\"\n        );\n\n       \n    }\n}\n\n```",
